eparate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y′ & =\\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{3}}{y} \\\\ y\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x & =\\int 5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\int 5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\frac{y^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{4}}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{y^{2}}{2}=\\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{4}}{4}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y^2 & =\\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{4}}{2}+2C \\\\ y & =\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{4}}{2}+2C} \\\\ y & =\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{4}}{2}+K}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=2C$ is an arbitrary real constant. Use either sign consistently on each interval where the radicand is positive." 13194139535980 17592186045443 true] [17592186551606 1080 "y=C + \\ln{\\left(\\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2} \\right)}" 13194139535980 17592186045443 true] [17592186551606 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535980 17592186045443 true] [17592186551606 1083 #uuid "1c425710-1266-581c-9722-fa8759833776" 13194139535980 17592186045443 true] [17592186551607 1080 "y=\\pm \\sqrt{C - \\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{4}}{2}}" 13194139535980 17592186045443 true] [17592186551607 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535980 17592186045443 true] [17592186551607 1083 #uuid "296f39b6-dbd2-59f0-a5e9-b253bd51c990" 13194139535980 17592186045443 true] [17592186551608 1080 "y=C + \\frac{4 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{3}}{3}" 13194139535980 17592186045443 true] [17592186551608 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535980 17592186045443 true] [17592186551608 1083 #uuid "2d258e30-3d6d-563a-8e22-e40f19619bec" 1319413953598